! C22-6578 PROBLEM 4.7, "TRANSPOSITION OF A 64 x 64 BIT MATRIX", printed
! p.40 (PDF 41), Method 1, read in the ink at 300 dpi.
!
!   "Given a 64x64 matrix whose elements are bits stored consecutively
!   and row-wise starting at BMX64.  Create the transpose and store it in
!   the same area."
!
!   "Method 1.  Bit-by-bit operation.  Same as Method 1 of previous
!   program with LOC and N redefined to be BMX64 and 64 respectively."
!
! SO THE PAGE PRINTS NO STATEMENTS FOR THIS METHOD.  The eighteen below
! are Problem 4.6 Method 1's, printed p.39, as printed there, with the two
! SYN cards redefined as the sentence says (each marked "printed (4.6):").
! problem_4_6_method1.strap has the reading and the page references.
! Assembled by the host STRAP II (ASM=strap2).  BMX64 is the deck's: 64
! words at 200.0-263.0, between guards at 199.0 and 264.0.
!
! N = 64 IS GENERAL IN EVERY PRINTED FIELD: XW2 = LOC+0.1 count 63;
! XW3 = LOC+0.N = LOC+1.0, the next row; VF = 0.1+0.64 = 1.1, one row
! and one bit; "N($3)" is 64 bits in a VFL address (an integer in a
! 24-bit field counts bits, C28-6129 Section I printed pp.8-9).  The
! inner loop exchanges A[i][j] and A[j][i], j = i+1..63, for rows i =
! 0..62: 2016 exchanges, each of the 2016 pairs above the diagonal once
! (the derivation for general N is in problem_4_6_method1.strap).
!
! THE DATA: 64 words drawn once from Python's random.Random(4707)
! (getrandbits(64), in order), written below; nothing in them is
! symmetric.  THE EXPECTED VALUES are worked by
! tests/verify_problem_4_matrix.py from the data as assembled and the
! statement (bit (r, c) to (c, r)), not from the model:
!   rows 0-63     the transpose, all 64 words.
!   x2 (18)       LOC + N*N bits = 264.0, count 0, refill XW22; XW22 the
!                 same word.
!   x3 (19)       LOC + N*N + N - 1 bits = 264.63, count 0, refill XW33;
!                 XW33 the same word.
!   acc_left (8)  bit 63 is A[63][62] as loaded, the last bit LF took
!                 from $3, and nothing else (the accumulator starts 0).
!   acc_right (9) bit 127 is A[62][63] as loaded.
!   guards        unchanged.  PC: the half word of the printed BEW.
!
! PASSED AGAINST THE MODEL AS IT STOOD.
!
! INJECTION, DATA SIDE, OBSERVED 2026-11-16:
!   the first word of BMX64 (16)09C4D5B1949524CB -> (16)01C4D5B1949524CB
!   (A[0][4] turned off), by --sub on the copy that runs; the expected words
!   are worked from the deck as it stands.  PREDICTED: row 4's bit 0.
!   OBSERVED: FAIL row04 only, (16)7A1A56121855F9EA for (16)FA1A56121855F9EA;
!   the other 63 rows, $2, $3, XW22, XW33, the accumulator, the guards
!   and the PC pass.

! --- printed p.39 (4.6 Method 1), LOC and N as p.40 redefines them ----
BMX8T   LX, $2, XW2; SX, $2, XW22
        LX, $3, XW3; SX, $3, XW33
LOF     LF(BU,1),0.0($3),64
        LF(BU,1), 0.0($2)
        SF(BU,1)(V+ICR),0.1($2),64
        SF(BU,1)(V+ICR),N($3)
        BZXCZ,LOF
        V+C,$2, VF; SX,$2,XW22
        V+C, $3, VF; SX, $3,XW33
        BZXCZ, LOF
        BEW,$
XW2     XW, LOC+0.1,N-1,XW22
XW3     XW,LOC+0.N,N-1, XW33
XW22    XW,0
XW33    XW,0
VF      VF,0.1+0.N
LOC     SYN, BMX64                      !printed (4.6): LOC SYN, BMATX8
N       SYN,64                          !printed (4.6): N SYN,8
! --- the deck's data ---------------------------------------------------
        SLC, 199.0
GUARD1  DD(BU,64),(16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
BMX64   DD(BU,64),(16)09C4D5B1949524CB
